message: "Please cite the technical report using the preferred citation below."
title: "Exact Mersenne Factor Censuses and a Finite Bernoulli Multiplicity Model"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Discovery099/mersenne-factor-laws"
authors:
  - family-names: Miki
    given-names: Chris
abstract: >-
  Bounded exact Mersenne factor censuses and a zero-fit comparison of established
  multiplicity heuristics. Two independent engines counted 487025 factor pairs
  over prime exponents from 10000001 through 30000000 with k at most 10000.
  External operator reviews confirm both sealed census comparisons. The report
  distinguishes the independent reviews from locally certified results and
  documents a residual discrepancy and a missing external pre-run timestamp
  for region 2. No new theorem, law or credited factor is claimed.
keywords:
  - Mersenne numbers
  - computational number theory
  - Poisson-binomial distribution
  - reproducibility
